Changelog: 17-10-2026 14:24:42

Release 0.1.6.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 13:46:57

Fixed. The app's folder in the suite is apps/acpi (was apps/persistent-acpi) and its package is locked_acpi (was
bc250_acpi_gui): the suite's naming convention (owner, 17-10-2026), a short folder name and a package name without
the BC-250 prefix; both names are the owner's. With the folder go its key in the portal, its chapter of the wiki
(apps/acpi/), its installer test and its release tags: acpi-v<x.y.z> from the next release on. The installed app
keeps its name, its launcher bc250-persistent-acpi-gui, its root-owned folder /opt/bc250-persistent-acpi (each
install replaces the whole folder, so no old package folder stays behind), its venv and its settings, and the ACPI
override on the board is not touched; the portal moves its record of the installed copy to the new key.

