Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:10:51

Release 0.1.3.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:01:27

instance.py follows core's: a second launch can hand its arguments to the running instance (already_running(app_id, args), serve(..., on_args)). This app passes none, so it behaves as before: a second launch shows the open window.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 00:23:49

images/bc250-persistent-acpi-128.png: the 128 px version of the icon, scaled from the 512 px file, so the app's images folder has both sizes like the other apps. Nothing uses it yet; it is the source for the portal's tile icon.

Changelog: 13-10-2026 15:53:27

Release 0.1.2.

Changelog: 13-10-2026 15:51:48

The installer installs the Python packages with pip --upgrade (owner's decision, 13-10-2026): installing again brings each package to the newest version its requirements allow, so a security fix within that range arrives with a reinstall from the portal.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 19:25:11

Release 0.1.1.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 19:02:46

instance.py, the copy of core's: Two launches at the same moment (a double-click on a Desktop icon that opens on one
click) no longer open two windows. Both found no running instance, since the window and its socket take a while to
appear, and the second then removed the first one's socket. The first launch now takes a lock file at once; a launch
that finds it taken waits up to 10 s for that instance's socket and hands over instead. A crashed instance's lock is
stale, so the next launch starts as before.

Changelog: 10-10-2026 20:56:48

Release 0.1.0. Initial release

Changelog: 09-10-2026 22:59:08

README: only the app's name, what it does and its license, with a link to its chapter of the manual; the rest moved into the manual (docs/apps/persistent-acpi.md).

Changelog: 09-10-2026 21:24:58

Tests: the window test waits for the status run to finish before it checks the idle states line; on a slow
runner the banner could change before that line had arrived.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 18:32:48

Docs: links to the old stand-alone repositories (which no longer exist) now point at the apps' folders in the
suite repository (README).

Changelog: 09-10-2026 17:51:51

Only one instance runs per user: starting the app again brings the running window to the front instead of opening a second one (bc250_core's instance module, copied into the package until the app moves onto core).

Changelog: 09-10-2026 16:10:58

New app icon (images/bc250-persistent-acpi.png), replacing the drawn one.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 13:56:58

The app now has a window: BC-250 Persistent ACPI (bc250_acpi_gui, PyQt6) shows whether the override is
installed, the CPU's frequency steps and idle states, and with Status with sudo whether the kernel loaded the
tables this boot. Install and Uninstall run the override script through sudo (masked password prompt, never
stored). A warning that asks "Continue anyway?" (no BC-250 GPU found, a BIOS that looks modded) is shown in a
dialog, and the install runs again with --yes only after Yes.

The override scripts moved into bc250-acpi-override.sh (--install, --uninstall, --status, --yes); the install
and uninstall steps are the same as in the old install.sh and uninstall.sh. Without a terminal, a warning stops
the install with exit code 3 instead of waiting for an answer. uninstall.sh is gone.

install.sh now installs the app like the other suite apps, as your own user: a root-owned copy in
/opt/bc250-persistent-acpi-v<version>, a venv with PyQt6, the launcher bc250-persistent-acpi-gui, an app menu
entry and a Desktop icon (--no-desktop-shortcut, --uninstall, --uninstall --purge). Installing the app changes
nothing on the board. Run as root, it stops and points at sudo ./bc250-acpi-override.sh --install.

New app icon, tests for the override script against a fake board and for the window, and README updated.

